  "articleBody": "It's a big question, and you're not alone if you're scratching your head about whether your land is suitable for a tiny home. The main thing people often miss is that tiny homes aren't just one-size-fits-all, especially when it comes to placement. You might think any plot of land works, but there's a lot more to it than just space. Things like local zoning, utility access, and even the topography of your land play a huge role. Maybe you're envisioning a tiny home on wheels, but your local regulations only permit foundation-built ADUs. Or perhaps you haven't considered how you'll get power and water to the site, or where drainage and septic systems will go. These aren't minor details; they're foundational to a successful tiny home placement. If these considerations feel overwhelming, that's a clear sign to reach out. We specialize in understanding these nuances, offering site plan services that cover land use planning, zoning, and utility assessments, so you can move forward with confidence.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-02"
}